.TH tty 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
tty \- print the name of this terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tty
[\fB\-s\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tty
prints the path of the terminal on standard input, or
.B not a tty
if standard input is a file or a pipe.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s
Print nothing; give the answer in the exit status alone.
.SH BUGS
The exit status is always 0, whether or not standard input is a
terminal, because the not-a-tty case is turned into that string before
the status is worked out.  So
.B \-s
tells you nothing, and a script must look at the output instead.
.PP
An extra blank line is printed after the name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stty (1),
.BR who (1),
.BR mesg (1)
